<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">East Africa Protectorate</h1><p class="st-meta">1895 CE – 1920 CE · capital Mombasa; later Nairobi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British protectorate that became Kenya, defined by the Uganda Railway and the arrival of European settlers in the highlands.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1895 the British government took over the territory between the coast and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-african-rift">Rift Valley</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imperial-british-east-africa-company">Imperial British East Africa Company</a>. The ten-mile coastal strip remained nominally part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Sultanate of Zanzibar</a>. The administration was based at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mombasa">Mombasa</a> until 1905, when the capital moved to Nairobi, a railway depot.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uganda-railway">Uganda Railway</a>, built from 1896 to 1901 largely by Indian indentured workers, opened the interior. Commissioner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-eliot-diplomat">Charles Eliot</a> encouraged white settlement in the fertile highlands, which were reserved for Europeans, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maasai-people">Maasai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kikuyu-people">Kikuyu</a> lost land and Africans were taxed and pressed into labour. Military expeditions subdued resisting peoples such as the Nandi.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1920 the interior was annexed as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kenya-colony">Kenya Colony</a> and the coastal strip became the Kenya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>. The settler-dominated order set up in these years shaped Kenyan politics up to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mau-mau-rebellion">Mau Mau uprising</a> and independence.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/east-africa-protectorate.jpg" alt="East Africa Protectorate" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday (talk) (Transfered by MSClaudiu/Original uploaded by Orange Tuesday) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kenya_(1895%E2%80%931921).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1895 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mombasa; later Nairobi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Arthur Hardinge, Charles Eliot</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion, Christianity, Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Swahili</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kenya">Kenya</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British East Africa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1908&amp;focus=east-africa-protectorate" aria-label="East Africa Protectorate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5781 2329 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where East Africa Protectorate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6101 2585L6101 2585M6101 2585L4997 651M6101 2585L6023 2482"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6101 2585h0M4997 651h0M6023 2482h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6101 2585h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6101 2585h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mombasa. <a href="/atlas?year=1908&amp;focus=east-africa-protectorate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
